---
/**
 * The nav wordmark's icon. This used to inline public/favicon.svg, on the
 * assumption it was a trace of the real app icon — it is not: rendered at
 * any size it's a mountain/rocket silhouette, unrelated to the actual
 * Moshpit/App/Assets.xcassets/AppIcon.appiconset/AppIcon.png (a tilted
 * glowing key over three idle ones — the app's own "one agent needs you"
 * motif). public/icon-192.png is that real icon, already exported at
 * 192×192 — plenty of headroom for the ~20px display size this renders at,
 * so no extra export step. The rounded-square mask is applied here via
 * border-radius rather than baked into the PNG, matching how the source
 * asset itself ships flat-square (iOS applies the squircle mask at the
 * OS/App-Store display layer, not in the icon file).
 */
---

<img class="mark" src="/icon-192.png" width="192" height="192" alt="" />
